The primary source of orcish arrows is other orcs.  You'll need to mow
them down in droves but you will end up with a lot of orcish arrows if
you are willing to do that and if you take care of your numerical
alignment as you go.  I kill a peaceful then count killing three
hostiles before I kill the next one.  In the meantime my pet kills
plenty of peacefuls.

> My question, then, is whether I'm better off focusing on dagger
> initially and saving my initial orcish (or elven) arrows until I can
> stop them from evaporating, or focusing on bow initially and hoping to
> replace my racial arrows later.

For ranger it does make sense to exercise daggers up to expert first
including naming Sting for use imn melee, then exercising your crowning
gift weapon. That's some time in the mines in a high preparation game.
Once you have completed the mines you have the luck stone so your luck
is maxed out. Then it makes sense to start exercising bow.


